      "side": 1,
      "message": "This causes a heap allocation, but in practice most clip stacks will only be a few elements that influence a given shape. It would be nice to use STArray with an N of 2-4-ish to keep the common clip stack\u0027s affecting elements in the stack of `Device::drawGeometry`.\n\nThat would require moving the `elements` to an out parameter. STArray subclasses TArray I believe, so this could still take the param as `TArray*`. I think that would also mean ClipStateForDraw would go away and this function would just return a Clip, and updateClipStateForDraw() would take a Clip and a span.",
